  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA dominates over image (0.485 vs 0.208), and within RNA, multi-profile + avgpool with PCA (config_002, acc 0.591) is clearly the best setup, beating both single-profile (0.485) and transformer aggregation (0.519). However, PCA is the only RNA encoder tested, so we cannot yet tell whether the learned representation quality is a bottleneck or whether the profile/aggregation design is the primary driver. Question: Does replacing PCA with the learned SCVI encoder (200-dim) improve performance when holding profile (multi) and aggregation (avgpool) fixed at their best-performing values? This isolates the encoder effect with a single-variable change from config_002. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly tests whether a more expressive RNA representation can push past the 0.591 ceiling, which determines whether subsequent multimodal experiments should pair a stronger encoder with image fusion. If SCVI matches or beats PCA, it justifies investing budget in multimodal configs with learned encoders; if it underperforms, PCA is sufficient and budget is better spent exploring fusion strategies. This is more informative than jumping to multimodal (where image's weakness confounds the fusion question) or testing image improvements (which seem unlikely to close the 0.38 gap to RNA)."
}

